The physical significance of the tangent line is this: 
Suppose a particle of mass m travels along a path x. 
If, suddenly, at t = t₀, all forces cease to act on the particle (so that, by Newton's second law of motion F = ma, we have a(t) ّّ= 0 for t >= t₀), then the particle will follow the tangent line path of equation 3. 
